{"connection_id": "BC-d8de1f78328f91972bd1", "ref": "WLC:Ps.119.122", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "God asked to stand surety", "note": "The psalmist asks God to be surety for the servant's good against oppressors; the commentary's kefil image extends here from a human promisor to divine protection."}
{"connection_id": "BC-cd859131c4a5c48d6882", "ref": "WLC:Ps.15.4", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "karsi_anlati", "basis": "vow kept despite personal cost", "note": "The commentary's Arabic lexicon gloss for root ʿ-ṣ-r (B006) describes giving a gift and then withdrawing it; Psalm 15 praises the person who swears to their own hurt and does not change, a direct counter-image of retracting one's word."}
{"connection_id": "BC-2198c8a365681c6c866c", "ref": "WLC:Ps.15.4", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "oath honored even at personal cost", "note": "The person fit to dwell with God swears to his own hurt and does not change his word; it clarifies the weight of the commentary's binding oath when keeping it becomes burdensome."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c22271089548679c4e7f", "ref": "WLC:Ps.2.7", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "Arabic ḥ-q-q / Hebrew ḥ-q-q; package table's sound correspondence, unverified", "note": "The commentary labels بِٱلْحَقّ with Arabic root ḥ-q-q and describes a binding right; the Hebrew king announces a חֹק, a decree, from the candidate root חקק, so the psalm shows a related legal sense without proving cognacy."}
{"connection_id": "BC-71e065072bc9ca20698d", "ref": "WLC:Ps.2.7", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "חקק sound correspondence; decree given to a son", "note": "The king recites the Lord's decree declaring him a son; Hebrew חֹק from the table connects a prescribed word to a father-son relation, though it is a royal oracle rather than an inheritance allotment."}
{"connection_id": "BC-07bd80fbe7f3f2f2b9d3", "ref": "WLC:Ps.2.8", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "son receives an inheritance", "note": "The royal son is promised the nations as his inheritance; this develops the commentary's image of a binding grant passing from a father to an heir."}
{"connection_id": "BC-385fc51ad88f1c93997b", "ref": "WLC:Ps.37.34", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "wait patiently and keep the way", "note": "The psalm calls its hearer to wait for the Lord and keep his way amid the wicked's apparent success; obedience and endurance are joined as in the commentary's final counsel."}
{"connection_id": "BC-eb88c7351d027fd670f0", "ref": "WLC:Ps.39.7", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "wealth heaped with unknown successor", "note": "Amid reflection on life's brevity, a person heaps up wealth without knowing who will gather it; this sharpens the commentary's concern to assign goods before death. Hebrew צבר here means heap, not Arabic sabr's patience."}
{"connection_id": "BC-515b821ab2fa4e4d4926", "ref": "WLC:Ps.71.18", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "old age and testimony to generations", "note": "The aging speaker asks to remain until he has told the coming generation of God's strength; this gives the commentary's deathbed image a living elder's explicit concern to pass testimony onward."}
{"connection_id": "BC-d23fe1c908e039f35236", "ref": "WLC:Ps.71.18", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "aged speaker tells the next generation", "note": "The aged psalmist asks not to be forsaken until he has declared God's power to the next generation; an approaching end makes transmission of testimony urgent."}
{"connection_id": "BC-6bd0c24e8e820a30825e", "ref": "WLC:Ps.78.37", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "אמנ sound correspondence; unfaithful covenant hearers", "note": "The generation instructed about God's deeds is said to be unfaithful to his covenant; Hebrew אמנ from the table supplies the contrary case to the commentary's inherited faithfulness."}
{"connection_id": "BC-d9904b580403ecca399b", "ref": "WLC:Ps.78.4", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "teaching the next generation", "note": "The speaker says the ancestors' deeds and praise of God will be told to the coming generation rather than hidden from their children; this makes the commentary's intergenerational handoff of truth a deliberate communal practice."}
{"connection_id": "BC-aeb1b4742e6a8587a0eb", "ref": "WLC:Ps.78.5", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "command fathers to teach children", "note": "God establishes testimony in Jacob and commands fathers to make it known to their children; the commentary's passed-on faith has a precise communal analogue."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ab79112e5aec837a151b", "ref": "WLC:Ps.78.6", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "children yet unborn tell their children", "note": "The next generation is to arise and tell its own children; this explicitly extends the chain beyond the first recipients of the bequest."}
{"connection_id": "BC-b5138aa411b3b377268c", "ref": "WLC:Ps.78.7", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "hope in God and keep commandments", "note": "The purpose of telling children is that they set hope in God, remember his works and keep his commands; transmitted faith and action are both named."}
{"connection_id": "BC-3bb2962ecfae620ff556", "ref": "WLC:Ps.89.2", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "Arabic ʾ-m-n / Hebrew ʾ-m-n; package table's sound correspondence, unverified", "note": "The commentary's root label for ءَامَنُوا۟ is Arabic ʾ-m-n; the psalm promises to tell God's אֱמוּנָה from generation to generation, joining faithfulness to the transmission of a spoken legacy."}
